WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.810
<i>I'm Hasegawa Kouta.</i>

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.230
<i>I'm a rather average high school
student with a bit of a secret.</i>

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.670
<i>One day, I had a not-so-average encounter.</i>

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.910
You don't mind using
the towel I just used, right?

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.010
Hey, breakfast is ready.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.000
Thanks.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.210
I'm off.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.380
Can't we go together sometime?

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.720
Riverside Kosugi Twin Towers First Building

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.390
Riverside Kosugi Twin Towers Second Building

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.830
Shunsuke, morning.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:45.630
Hey.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.270
Shall we go then?

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.570
Shunsuke's Place

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.570
Yuu's Place

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.230
Roger that.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.950
Gift Gate After the Rain

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.280
Oh, that's right,

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.240
you don't know, do you, Hase?

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:57.780
No...

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.200
Mizuno Yuu from Class 2-4.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.250
He's flashy and kind of a jokester,

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.070
but he's cheerful and friendly so he's
pretty popular with both girls and guys.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.850
Yoshino Shunsuke is in the same class.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.170
He's the ace striker of the soccer team.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.200
The silent and stoic type,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.120
he's really popular with both girls and guys,
along with Student Council President Minamoto.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:25.390
They're pretty famous around here
for being big fans of Sanrio characters.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.030
They weren't exactly hiding it, were they?

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.760
<i>They're really open about it...</i>

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.710
That's it, they use it for attention!

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.100
"We love cute things, too."

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:41.260
They use that to make girls swoon, don't they?!

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.230
Like I'm gonna let them!
Damn them, that's unfair!

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:47.920
That has nothing to do with it, they were
more popular than you even before that.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.410
Anyway, it's probably the opposite.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:57.010
No matter how cool they are,
there are still plenty of people

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.840
who think it's weird for guys
to have those interests.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.980
It's normal to feel like that, isn't it?

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.400
Hase?

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:09.900
N-Nothing, you're right!
I'm not interested at all!

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:14.280
Oops, sorry. I'm thirsty so I'm
gonna go buy something to drink!

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.280
I guess I was too pushy...

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.040
Mackerel Cola

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:25.040
Why are they selling such a weird thing here?!

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.950
I've gotta stop being so careless.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.970
That's how things wound up
like they did yesterday, too.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:37.560
Yo, Kouta.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.720
M-Mizuno and Yoshino?!

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.510
You called me Kouta?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:48.150
Huh? It was Hasegawa Kouta, right?

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.430
Yeah, you're right, but...

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.590
Then we're good!

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.680
Which means it's fine if you call me Yuu.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.120
You can call him Shushu, too.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.610
Don't decide that yourself.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.370
Anyway, Kouta, about yesterday...

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:06.870
You were trying to be careful so no one
would find out that I like her, weren't you?

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.250
Y-Yeah...

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:12.960
But in the end, I guess I really
didn't need to though.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.900
I thought so!

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:19.170
You might have been a little clumsy
about it, but it made me happy.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.040
Huh?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.730
I'm saying that you're a good person.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.070
Wh-What's with that?

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:33.500
Something similar happened
to me a long time ago.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.810
That's all.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.610
So you had something like that, too?

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.790
Well, in my case it wasn't My Melody though.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.320
You're...

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.910
You're pretty familiar
with My Melody for a guy.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.500
Hey,

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:59.380
does that mean you actually
like Sanrio characters like we do?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.800
Oh, class is starting! See ya!

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.840
Hey, wait! Kouta!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.050
They figured me out. I knew it.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:14.770
Ugh, why am I always so careless?!

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.690
What are you doing, Kouta?

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.150
Ow...

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.250
Mom! Don't just come into my room!

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:30.470
Well, I was trying to tell you
dinner was ready, but you didn't...

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:31.850
Huh?

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.910
I haven't seen this in a while,
where did you get it?

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.000
I just found it.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.760
This was your favorite thing, Kouta.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.610
It's not food, don't say it like that.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:49.560
But you used to fall asleep
sucking on its ear every night.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.730
Do you still need it?

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:53.630
I'm in high school!

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:55.440
I don't need it at all!

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.630
Okay then! You said it's
dinner time, let's go!

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.550
Gosh, you don't have to push me like that.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.260
Oh, a wild Kouta.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.530
M-Mizuno?

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.750
I told you to call me Yuu.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.780
You're hurting my feelings
a bit with that attitude by the way.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:24.510
Sorry...

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:31.210
Then, I request you come with me after
school to Gift Gate as an apology!

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.850
Why would I do that?!

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.140
Oh, come on, let's go.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:38.350
They get new products in today!

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:43.110
I'm not interested in Sanrio goods though.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.790
How do you know what
kind of store Gift Gate is?

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.440
I only mentioned new products.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.020
That's not fair...

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:04.030
Well, I didn't think it'd go that well...

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.810
You're way too easy, Kouta.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.090
Well, excuse me.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:10.260
What's the harm? Come with me.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:16.070
There aren't many guys who like Sanrio,

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:18.460
and when girls see Melody-chan,

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.950
they let their guard down
when you talk to them.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.530
So you're after girls.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.080
No, I'm just joking, mostly.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.070
Then you're mostly serious.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.620
What I'm actually after is the new products!

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:36.090
I want to enhance my lovely
Melody-chan collection.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:47.680
What's wrong?

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:49.610
I'm not going.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:56.530
I don't like Sanrio at all.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:03.420
Man, I got dumped.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:04.630
Of course you did.

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:07.220
You did that on purpose.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:08.810
What?

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:11.270
You always stick your nose in
without reading the situation.

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:13.880
Being pushy isn't a good thing.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:17.910
There's not many who share our interests,
so I just want to hurry and be friends.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.660
Don't you feel the same, Shunsuke?

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.030
I'm not interested.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:24.330
Dealing with people is a pain.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:26.300
I'm good with the people I'm stuck with.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.550
I get it, so you're saying
you're fine with just me.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:34.710
Oh my, are you jealous, Shushu?

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.260
That's what you think.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.920
Listen, that guy—

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.070
Stop! I don't want to hear it!

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:12.250
You're Hasegawa from class 2-3, right?

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:14.180
Yes?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.010
S-Student council president?!

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.190
Um, do you need something?

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:22.260
You don't need to be so stiff.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:25.940
You just had such a serious
expression that it worried me.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.070
Oh... sorry about that.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:31.050
I'm fine though.

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:33.070
Okay then, if you're sure.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:37.490
If anything should come up though, you're welcome
to come by the student council room anytime.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.880
Well, I'm probably being
unnecessarily nosey though.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.580
Not at all!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.460
Thank you.

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:47.270
No problem, be careful going home.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.180
You're Nishimiya Ryo, right?

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:02.670
H-How do you know my name?

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.210
It's my job as the student council president.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.790
Anyway, you're always enthusiastically
observing things, aren't you?

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:13.140
N-Not really, I was just killing time.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.650
It's not like I'm interested. See ya.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:16.660
Nishimiya.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.090
You can come kill time any time.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:34.920
I love you and Purin, Grandma!

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.110
I'm so glad.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:41.230
I love you and Purin-chan very, very much.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:45.490
Then, I love you very,
very, very, very, very much!

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:46.290
Oh, my.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.970
A dream...?

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:07.620
Damn it, why am I having
a dream like that now?

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.070
The weather is pretty awful...

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.840
Cloudy then rain

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.310
I wonder if Mizuno will bug me today, too.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.040
Dang it...

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:45.670
I'm home.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.080
Welcome home!

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:49.530
So you made it through the rain okay.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:51.960
Yeah, I was able to make it
back before it started falling.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:56.510
Oh, that reminds me, I took care
of the trash in your room.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.550
I told you not to just go in my room!

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:05.560
I wound up not seeing Mizuno at all today.

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:09.770
Not that it matters anyway...

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:13.100
Huh?

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:16.190
P-Purin's gone?

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:24.540
Mom!

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.500
What? We're having gratin for dinner.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:28.780
Not that!

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:31.540
Do you know where the Purin from my room is?

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:32.810
Purin?

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:35.410
Oh, the stuffed animal.

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:42.210
You had thrown it away
so I sent it off with the recyclers.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.860
No! I wouldn't just throw it away!

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:47.250
Really?

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:50.680
But you said you didn't need it anymore.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.580
That's not what I meant...

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.310
Damn it!

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.910
E-Excuse me!

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:06.280
Have you seen the recycling truck around here?

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:11.970
I see... thank you.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:46.350
<i>Where?</i>

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:49.240
<i>Where is it?</i>

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:54.880
<i>We've... always been together.</i>

00:12:57.430 --> 00:13:00.410
<i>It was a gift from a special person.</i>

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:04.410
<i>It's my precious... precious...</i>

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:22.600
Grandma...

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:31.030
Come on, Kou-chan. You can get up yourself.

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:34.650
Grandma, Grandma!

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:36.850
It's all right,

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:39.520
you can do it, Kou-chan.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:41.040
Huh?

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.930
See, you did it!

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.600
It's just like I said,

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.860
you can do anything, Kou-chan.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:06.210
Yeah!

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:14.630
I... can't...

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:22.510
I can't... do anything...

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.260
Whatcha doing, Kouta?

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:32.170
Mizuno?

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:34.770
Hey now, you okay there?

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.110
It doesn't matter anymore...

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.750
It's all my fault.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.190
If I was more like you,
none of this would've happened...

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:52.120
Don't really get what's going on,
but two Yuu's would suck.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.030
Hey, Shushu, what's that supposed to mean?

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:58.780
I had someone I loved and something I loved.

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:01.670
I used to be able to admit that so easily.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:07.300
But, somewhere along the way,
saying that got to be embarrassing.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:16.350
I did something that I couldn't take back.

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:24.060
I'm so pathetic and miserable.

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:29.740
That's why I could never
look you in the eye, Mizuno.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:31.740
Kouta...

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:33.370
How?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:39.200
How can you admit that
you love things so easily

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.560
and not be ashamed?!

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:48.510
I can't do it! I can't...

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.980
The sooner I forget about what I've lost,

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:56.060
maybe things will get easier?

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:03.970
I honestly don't get what you're talking about,

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.750
so this might seem a little insensitive...

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.280
What's so wrong with admitting
that you like the things you like?

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.190
I love My Melody.

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:17.830
And not just My Melody;

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:22.620
I love my family, girls, my friends,
Shunsuke, and you, Kouta.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:25.130
I really love them.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.000
Mizuno...

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:31.480
Y'know, Kouta...

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:40.810
There's absolutely nothing to be
ashamed of in loving something!

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.410
So why don't you tell me, too?

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:51.400
I'm not going to laugh or make fun of you,

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:55.260
so tell me what you love.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:02.360
I... I....

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:05.130
I—

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:08.840
I love my grandma!

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:12.160
I love the Pompompurin
that my grandma gave me!

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:15.800
I've loved it for so, so long!

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:21.420
Then, let's go, Kouta.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:35.450
Okada Recycling

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:35.450
All Household Appliances
Furniture/Bedding

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:35.460
I got us permission.

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:39.660
We can look through things as much
as we want, as long as we clean up afterwards.

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.620
Thanks, Yoshino.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:43.770
Thank you for your help, too, Mizuno.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:46.600
You told us about how desperate you are.

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:49.460
This is the only place where
the recycling for the area goes.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.880
With a little checking,
you could have figured that out.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:54.630
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:59.770
Let's get searching for Kouta's Pompompurin!

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:01.320
You don't have to do that...

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.560
It's totally fine. 
We'll see this through with you.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:07.610
Okay.

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.450
Okada Recycling

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.450
All Household Appliances,
Furniture/Bedding

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.330
Purin, come here!

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:52.540
You've gotten so beat up...

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:56.680
I guess you've been like
that for a while though.

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:06.750
I'm sorry, I love you.

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:19.780
You seem to be in a pretty
good mood today, Hase.

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:22.010
You think so? I guess I am.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:26.420
I'm more worried about that than you though.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:32.350
Oh, I got this from that girl when I
was hanging out with you guys the other day.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:38.160
Since she gave it to me, 
I figured I should use it—

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.180
That's not it.

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:42.200
I like it.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.160
What do you like?

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:51.090
<i>Grandma said I could do anything.</i>

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.290
<i>So, I'm going to start over from here.</i>

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:59.010
<i>First, I'll start by properly saying
that I like the things I like.</i>

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.640
I've kept quiet about it until now

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:04.860
but the truth is I like it.

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:07.800
Pompompurin.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:18.570
<b>Factoid: The Musashi-Kosugi Gift Gate is
the image at the top of Sanrio's store introduction page.</b>

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:15.860
Are we really going in, Mizuno?

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:21.780
Oh, I-I mean... Y-Yuu.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.500
Of course.

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:27.600
What are you hesitating for now
when we're already here?

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:31.470
It'll be fine, nothing's going
to change by going in.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:34.330
You might turn out like Yuu though.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:37.290
Hey, Shushu, you don't need to say that.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:40.090
Come on, let's go, Kouta.

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:42.730
Okay.

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:02.870
You're right, nothing changed.

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:04.320
Right?

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:06.330
Purin's so cute!

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:09.410
No, Kitty-san is obviously cuter.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:13.450
Well, that just means they're
all cute including Melody-chan.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:16.830
Now then, let the shopping commence!

00:23:00.930 --> 00:23:02.930
I used up all my allowance.

00:23:02.930 --> 00:23:04.320
You had too much fun.

00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:06.740
I'll have to get another job—

00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:09.490
Yuu?

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:11.570
Yuri-chan, something wrong?

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:19.030
That's so disgusting.

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:22.610
Um... wh-who are you?

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:23.250
You're supposed to be boys.

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.680
Aren't you ashamed of yourself,

00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:28.340
Brother?

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:29.430
Huh?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
Next Episode

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.880
Next time, "My Sister Blue."
